.\" Manpage for tarpit-honeypot.
.\" Render: man ./docs/tarpit-honeypot.1   Install: cp to /usr/share/man/man1/
.TH TARPIT-HONEYPOT 1 "2026-05-21" "tarpit-honeypot 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tarpit-honeypot \- CGO-free deception + detection honeypot sensor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tarpit-honeypot
.RI [ global-flags ]
.I subcommand
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B tarpit-honeypot
.BR --version | -V
.br
.B tarpit-honeypot
.BR help " [" \fIsubcommand\fR | \fItopic\fR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tarpit-honeypot
is a single, statically linked, CGO-free Go binary that stands up
plausible decoy services (SSH, HTTP/S, FTP, SMB, RDP, databases, a large
set of ICS/OT protocols, printers/MFDs, remote-access and out-of-band
management endpoints), records every interaction as a structured event,
and forwards alerts to one or more outbound channels. It never exposes a
real shell, filesystem, or exploitable code path: dangerous operations are
recognized and logged, never performed.
.PP
An optional
.I archetype
pins every fingerprint-bearing handler to a single coherent device
identity (banners, SNMP identity, MAC OUI, TLS posture, ICMP TTL, web UI,
advertised CVEs) so a scanner cannot catch the sensor on an internal
inconsistency. See
.BR "tarpit-honeypot list-archetypes" " and " docs/archetypes.md .
.SH GLOBAL FLAGS
.TP
.BR --version ", " -V
Print version, commit, and build date, then exit.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Print the subcommand index.
.SH COMMON FLAGS
Most subcommands accept the shared logging and config-override set.
.TP
.BI -c " path"
Config file (default
.IR /etc/tarpit-honeypot/config.yaml ).
Repeatable to combine files.
.TP
.BI --set " key.path=value"
Override one YAML key (repeatable; type auto-detected). Applied last.
.TP
.BI -i ", " --interface " name"
Network interface for the AF_PACKET layer (repeatable).
.TP
.BI --log-level " level"
.BR debug | info | warn | error
(default
.BR info ).
.TP
.BI --log-format " fmt"
.BR text | json
(default
.BR text ).
.TP
.BI --log-file " path"
Redirect logs to a file (default stderr).
.TP
.BR --quiet ", " --verbose
Shortcuts for
.B --log-level=error
and
.BR --log-level=debug .
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Start the sensor (listeners + sinks). Reloads config on
.BR SIGHUP ;
.B --dry-run
loads and validates without binding.
.TP
.B validate-config
Parse and validate a config; with
.B --diff
classify hot-reloadable vs restart-required changes between two configs.
.TP
.B show-config
Print the effective post-defaults config as YAML (secrets stay as env-var
names).
.TP
.B test-alert
Emit a synthetic event through the configured channels.
.TP
.B list-events
Tail / query events from the local SQLite store or JSON logs
.RB ( --since ", " --source ", " --rule ", " --limit ).
.TP
.B gen-token
Print an unguessable canary token
.RB ( --type " " dns | url | hex ).
.TP
.B export-pcap
Copy one event's per-connection pcap out of the captures directory.
.TP
.B list-honeynets
Print the configured artificial networks, hosts, and services.
.TP
.B list-devices
Print the learned-device inventory
.RI ( devices.json );
.B --json
for a baseline snapshot.
.TP
.B list-archetypes
Print the device/OS archetype catalog; add a name for the full
fingerprint, or
.BR --json .
.TP
.B list-handlers
Print the protocol handlers valid in a listener
.RB ( --proto " " tcp | udp ).
.TP
.B list-cves
Print the CVE catalog used for emulation + exploit detection
.RB ( --service ", " --json ).
.TP
.B list-techniques
Print the MITRE ATT&CK / D3FEND coverage map
.RB ( --kind " " rule | handler | anomaly ).
.TP
.B identify
Run the offline fingerprint engine over a supplied User-Agent, path, SSH
client id, JA3, or payload
.RB ( --ua ", " --ssh ", " --ja3 ", " --payload ", " --handler ).
.TP
.B init
Write a default config skeleton to stdout (or
.BR -o ).
.TP
.B completion
Print a shell-completion script
.RB ( bash | zsh | fish ).
.TP
.B help
Long-form help for a subcommand or topic
.RB ( "help archetypes" ).
.TP
.B version
Print version info.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/tarpit-honeypot/config.yaml
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I <data_dir>/events.db
SQLite event store (powers
.B list-events
and the web UI).
.TP
.I <data_dir>/devices.json
Learned-device inventory.
.TP
.I <data_dir>/captures/<event_id>.pcap
Per-connection packet captures (when
.B capture: true
is set on a listener).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Validate a config and start the sensor:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tarpit-honeypot validate-config -c /etc/tarpit-honeypot/config.yaml
tarpit-honeypot run -c /etc/tarpit-honeypot/config.yaml
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inspect the built-in catalogs offline:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tarpit-honeypot list-archetypes xerox-versalink
tarpit-honeypot list-cves --service ipp
tarpit-honeypot list-techniques --kind anomaly
.fi
.RE
.PP
Triage a captured signal:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tarpit-honeypot identify --ua "sqlmap/1.7" --payload '${jndi:ldap://x/a}'
.fi
.RE
.SH SECURITY
The sensor is read-only by design and never becomes an
amplification/reflection primitive or an exploitable target. The one
opt-in write path (web-UI device delete/whitelist) is gated by a config
flag plus an auth token. Run it as an unprivileged user; use
.B sensor.drop_user
/
.B sensor.drop_group
to drop privileges after binding low ports.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation in the
.I docs/
directory:
.IR README.md ", " docs/cli.md ", " docs/config.md ", " docs/usage.md ", "
.IR docs/archetypes.md ", " docs/design.md ", " docs/hardening.md ", "
.IR docs/INTEGRATIONS.md .
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/rom/tarpit-honeypot/issues .
